{"id": "EUVD-2026-86400", "enisaUuid": "eaa251a9-388c-358c-903f-bd61a8521685", "description": "ServiceNow has remediated an authorization bypass security issue that was identified in the ServiceNow AI Platform. This security issue, if exploited, could enable an unauthenticated user to access data within the ServiceNow AI Platform that the user otherwise would not be entitled to access, potentially enabling further unintended access.\n\n\n\n\n\nServiceNow deployed a security update to hosted instances and ServiceNow provided the update to our partners and self-hosted customers. We are not currently aware of malicious exploitation against ServiceNow instances. We recommend customers promptly apply appropriate updates or upgrade to a patched release if they have not already done so.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T18:52:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T19:16:40", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB3159623"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hv69-7jxx-r484", "CVE-2026-86859"], "assigner": "SN", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37ac537e-a21d-3ac2-902b-f32e8ba24bbf", "product": {"name": "ServiceNow AI Platform", "vendor": {"name": "Servicenow"}}, "product_version": "0 <Australia Patch 4 Hot Fix 3"}, {"id": "3e7afe7d-288a-38d2-aedf-b60289418969", "product": {"name": "ServiceNow AI Platform", "vendor": {"name": "Servicenow"}}, "product_version": "0 <Australia Patch 5"}, {"id": "4aaf5585-25f7-34c6-98bf-307143b19bef", "product": {"name": "ServiceNow AI Platform", "vendor": {"name": "Servicenow"}}, "product_version": "0 <Zurich Patch 10 Hot Fix 4a W32"}, {"id": "7f690332-e1e2-3dce-9801-421f05c542b9", "product": {"name": "ServiceNow AI Platform", "vendor": {"name": "Servicenow"}}, "product_version": "0 <Zurich Patch 10 Hot Fix 3b"}, {"id": "c2339ff3-e841-3de4-90e5-fb0b5ed2af7f", "product": {"name": "Service